  "name": "Multi-actor CHEFS form approval",
  "description": "## What it does\n\nStarts two Workflow Interaction Layer **Show Form** actions, merges their branches, and pauses at **Multi Webhook Wait Node** until callbacks identified by `actor=alice` and `actor=bob` have both arrived. **Process Results** is a NoOp placeholder for downstream result handling.\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Replace the example actor email addresses on both WIL nodes.\n2. Select a **Workflow Interaction Layer API** credential and a **CHEFS Form Authentication** credential on each WIL action; Show Form requires both.\n3. Ensure the runtime has `N8N_BASE_URL` and `INTERNAL_AUTH_TOKEN` for Multi Webhook Wait registration.\n4. While editing, POST to `/webhook-test/approval-trigger`, or activate the workflow and POST to `/webhook/approval-trigger`.\n\n## Notes\n\nThe callback expressions are `$execution.resumeUrl + '&actor=alice'` and `$execution.resumeUrl + '&actor=bob'`. The WIL nodes explicitly use Action / Create, User actor type, and POST callbacks. The wait resumes only after all expected callbacks arrive; see the [Multi Webhook Wait documentation](https://bcgov.github.io/common-hosted-workflow/community-nodes/multi-webhook-wait) for results and timeout cleanup. No credentials or pinned execution data are included.",
